# The to-do list itself. Real tasks about real, named people: probation
# reviews, salary conversations, contract dates, personal objectives. It is the
# private half of this repo and it never leaves the machine.
todo.md

# Written by the board before its first save of each run. Same content as
# todo.md, so same reason.
backups/
todo-backup-*.md

# The Obsidian views. Dataview Serializer fills these in with the tasks the
# queries match, so the file ends up holding the list as well. The queries
# themselves are committed as views.template.md.
views.md

# Obsidian's own state, if the folder is ever opened as a vault.
.obsidian/
.trash/

# The board writes todo.md via a temp file and swaps it in. If it ever crashes
# mid-write, this is left behind holding the whole list.
todo.md.tmp
*.md.tmp

# Anything scratch, in case a working copy of the list is ever parked here.
*.local.md
scratch/

# macOS and Python noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
